---
/**
 * PARENT ORIENTATION — the movement below the banner.
 *
 * ⚠ THE BANNER IS THE SHARED PageHero AND IS NOT TOUCHED HERE. A previous
 * version of this page replaced it with a bespoke cinematic hero. That was
 * wrong: the Academics banner is a locked global component, and the creativity
 * starts underneath it. This file therefore begins at section 01, and the page
 * file owns the banner.
 *
 * ⚠ FOUR SECTIONS. The bespoke hero's poster headline and standfirst went with
 * it; what remains is the story — before → scale → what happens → what follows.
 *
 * ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
 * EVERY FACT IS READ OFF sunbeamballia.edu.in/orientation/ OR OFF THE SCHOOL'S
 * OWN PROGRAMME POSTERS, NOW IN assets/school-event/Parent-Orientation/.
 *
 *   POSTER · 1st Parent's Orientation Programme, Session 2024-25:
 *     "17th January 2024 · Classes Nur. to IX & XI ·
 *      Strength - 234 Students with 389 Parents"
 *   POSTER · 5th, Session 2024-25:
 *     "11th March 2024 · Classes Nur. to IX & XI ·
 *      Strength - 61 Students with 104 Parents"
 *   POSTER · 1st, Session 2026-27:
 *     "18th January 2026 · Class Nur. to IX · 292 Students Appeared"
 *   POSTER · 3rd (header reads Session 2025-26):
 *     "14th February 2026 · Classes Nur. to IX"
 *   PAGE TEXT · 3rd, 2024-25: "strength of 109 students on 14/02/24".
 *   PAGE TEXT · 2024-25 first: organised "to get them acquainted with the
 *     curriculum and norms of the school."
 *   PAGE TEXT · 2026-27: the school "shared its vision for shaping young minds
 *     and highlighted its commitment to holistic education, discipline, and
 *     overall student growth."
 *   PAGE TEXT · standing note: parents who missed one are asked to submit the
 *     form before the last date "to participate in the next orientation process
 *     for their child."
 *   RESULT DOCUMENT · read directly: 12 pages, 18 January 2026, columns
 *     S.No. | Class | Form No. | Candidate Name | Father's Name | Form
 *     Submitted Y/N | Attendance | Remarks. Remarks read GRANTED / NOT GRANTED.
 *     292 rows — matching the poster's "292 Students Appeared".
 *
 * ⚠⚠ 234 AND 389 ARE FROM ONE POSTER AND ONE MORNING. The brief suggested
 * "260+ / 336+"; neither figure appears anywhere on the school's site, and the
 * "+" would be an invention on top of an invention. No number here is rounded
 * and none carries a plus.
 *
 * ⚠ THE FOUR STEPS IN §03 ARE NOT THE FOUR THE BRIEF SUGGESTED. "Parents
 * Interface Session", "Multiple Intelligence Stations", "Parent–Child
 * Participation" and "Leadership Interaction" were searched across
 * /orientation/, /school-activities/, /event-chronicles/ and
 * /event-chronicles-main/. None appears anywhere. The four below are what the
 * school's own photographs and result document evidence — a stronger set,
 * precisely because each can be checked.
 *
 * ⚠⚠ THE RESULT PDFs ARE DESCRIBED AND NOT LINKED. They publish roughly three
 * hundred children by name with their father's name and whether admission was
 * granted. Client decision, taken explicitly. docs/07 § C5 is still open.
 *
 * ⚠ EVERY PHOTOGRAPH WAS OPENED AND LOOKED AT BEFORE IT WAS CAPTIONED, and
 * seven downloaded frames that could not be verified were deleted rather than
 * captioned blind. Nothing here is a generic school photograph.
 *
 * MOTION — data-clip (wipe), data-count-dur (two speeds), data-drift (per-item),
 * data-draw (timeline), plus the site's data-mask / data-zoom / data-parallax.
 * All behind the existing prefers-reduced-motion and Save-Data gates.
 */
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import type { ImageMetadata } from 'astro';
import { getSchool } from '../../lib/cms';

/* All six verified by eye before use. */

/* ⚠ two-stars.png IS NOT IMPORTED HERE, deliberately. It is referenced from
   another component's CSS by url(), and handing it to astro:assets would make
   it emit as .webp and 404 that stylesheet — the exact failure dot-bg.png hit.
   star.png has no CSS references anywhere, so it is safe to import. */
import oStar from '../../assets/icons/star.png';
import { getAcademicTopic } from '../../lib/cms';
import SmartImage from '../ui/SmartImage.astro';

const ac = await getAcademicTopic('/academics/parent-partnership/parent-orientation/');
const pPrecept = ac.pic('pPrecept');
const pClassWide = ac.pic('pClassWide');
const pDeskTwo = ac.pic('pDeskTwo');
const pDeskFamily = ac.pic('pDeskFamily');

const school = await getSchool();

const S = school.name;

/* Resolved here rather than in the data, because astro:assets has to see each
   import statically to emit the AVIF/WebP variants. */
const stepPhoto = ac.section('stepPhoto').byKey;

/* key → alt text, rebuilt from the labelled rows the CMS stores. */
const frameAlt = Object.fromEntries(ac.section('frameAlt').details.map((d) => [d.k, d.v]));

/* Only programmes whose date is on the school's own poster or page text. */
const timeline = ac.section('timeline').details;

/* ⚠ FOUR FRAMES, BECAUSE THE REFERENCE HAS FOUR IMAGE POSITIONS. The morning
   has three photographed movements, so the fourth position takes a second frame
   of the one-to-one movement — a different family at a different desk, which is
   what the school's own photographs actually show — rather than being collapsed
   away or filled with an unrelated school picture. It carries a caption and no
   step number, so the 01/02/03 sequence stays honest. */
/* The lead time, as a visual rather than a sentence: orientation runs in these
   three months, and the session it admits to starts after them. The months are
   the school's own dates — 17 Jan, 14 Feb, 11 Mar, 18 Jan, 14 Feb. */
const months = ac.section('months').details;

/**
 * ⚠ `slot` IS THE LAYOUT KEY AND `cap` IS THE PHOTOGRAPH'S. The source card was
 * { key, photo, n, t, m }; the point keeps the first as `slot` and the second as
 * `cap`, so the four framed panels still find their own picture and caption.
 */
const frames = ac.section('frames').points;
const frame = (slot: string) => frames.find((f) => f.slot === slot)!;

---

{/* ══ 01 · BEFORE THE FIRST DAY ═════════════════════════════════════════════ */}
<section class="po-open" aria-labelledby="po-open-title" data-draw-scope>
  <div class="u-container po-open__grid">
    <div class="po-open__copy">
      <p class="po-eyebrow" data-reveal>Why it matters</p>

      <h2 class="po-open__h" id="po-open-title">
        <span data-clip data-clip-delay="0">Before the first day,</span>
        <span data-clip data-clip-delay="120">we begin</span>
        <span data-clip data-clip-delay="240"><em>together.</em></span>
      </h2>

      <p class="po-lede" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="140">
        Orientation at Sunbeam is not held in the first week of term. The school runs it again and
        again through the admission season — and tells families so directly: parents who miss one
        are asked to submit the form before the last date
        <em>“to participate in the next orientation process for their child.”</em>
      </p>

      {/* The school's own sentence, set as the display quote it deserves. */}
      <blockquote class="po-quote" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="220">
        <p>“To get them acquainted with the <em>curriculum and norms</em> of the school.”</p>
        <cite>The school’s account of its first orientation programme</cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>

    {/* Two frames, overlapped and at different scales — not one photograph in a
        box beside the copy. */}
    <div class="po-open__media">
      <span class="po-open__dots" aria-hidden="true"></span>

      <figure class="po-open__frame" data-mask data-zoom data-zoom-to="1.08">
        <SmartImage
          file={pPrecept}
          alt={ac.picAlt('pPrecept')}
         
          widths={[640, 1000, 1400]}
          sizes="(max-width: 1000px) 92vw, 46vw"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
        <figcaption>The PRECEPT syllabus, shown to parents before the session begins.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="po-open__inset" data-parallax data-parallax-y="26">
        <SmartImage
          file={pDeskTwo}
          alt={ac.picAlt('pDeskTwo')}
         
          widths={[280, 480]}
          sizes="(max-width: 1000px) 44vw, 20vw"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>

  {/* ── the lead time, drawn ────────────────────────────────────────────────
      This is section 01's answer to "how far before?", and it is a graphic
      rather than a clause in a paragraph. */}
  <div class="u-container po-lead">
    <p class="po-lead__cap" data-reveal>Orientation runs in</p>
    <div class="po-lead__rail" aria-hidden="true"><span class="po-lead__line" data-draw></span></div>
    <ol class="po-lead__row">
      {months.map((x) => (
        <li class="po-lead__item" data-drift="20">
          <span class="po-lead__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <p class="po-lead__m">{x.m}</p>
          <p class="po-lead__d">{x.d}</p>
        </li>
      ))}
      <li class="po-lead__item po-lead__item--end" data-drift="20">
        <span class="po-lead__dot po-lead__dot--end" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <p class="po-lead__m po-lead__m--end">…then the session begins</p>
        <p class="po-lead__d">Months later, not the week before</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

{/* ══ 02 · IN NUMBERS + TIMELINE ════════════════════════════════════════════ */}
<section class="po-num" aria-labelledby="po-num-title" data-draw-scope>
  <div class="u-container">
    <div class="po-num__head">
      <p class="po-eyebrow" data-reveal>1st Parent’s Orientation Programme · 17 January 2024</p>
      <h2 class="po-num__h" id="po-num-title" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="80">
        The morning, <em>counted</em>
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="po-num__stage">
      <div class="po-num__fig po-num__fig--a">
        {/* ⚠ 1.5s AGAINST 2.2s. Identical speeds read as one animation with two
            labels; a small difference makes them read as two facts arriving. */}
        <p class="po-num__n t-tabular"><span data-count="234" data-count-dur="1.5">234</span></p>
        <p class="po-num__l">Students</p>
      </div>

      <figure class="po-num__frame" data-zoom data-zoom-to="1.1">
        <SmartImage
          file={pClassWide}
          alt={ac.picAlt('pClassWide')}
         
          widths={[560, 900]}
          sizes="(max-width: 900px) 92vw, 38vw"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </figure>

      <div class="po-num__fig po-num__fig--b">
        <p class="po-num__n t-tabular"><span data-count="389" data-count-dur="2.2">389</span></p>
        <p class="po-num__l">Parents</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="po-num__note" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="120">
      More than three adults for every two children — and both figures come from the same poster
      for the same morning. The school counts parents separately from students, and the gap
      between the two is the most telling thing on it.
    </p>

    {/* The five published programmes, on one drawn line. */}
    <div class="po-tl">
      <p class="po-tl__cap" data-reveal>Every programme the school has published</p>
      <div class="po-tl__rail" aria-hidden="true"><span class="po-tl__line" data-draw></span></div>
      <ol class="po-tl__list">
        {timeline.map((t) => (
          <li class="po-tl__item" data-drift="18">
            <span class="po-tl__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <p class="po-tl__when t-tabular">{t.when}</p>
            <p class="po-tl__n">{t.n} Programme</p>
            <p class="po-tl__d">{t.detail}</p>
            <p class="po-tl__c">{t.classes}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{/* ══ 03 · WHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENS ════════════════════════════════════════════ */}
{/* Built to the client's reference as a blueprint. Its geometry was measured
    off the supplied image and normalised to a 1440 content width: four images
    at 12-column positions 1, 4, 7 and 10, three columns wide each, all at 4:5,
    with image B 60px below image A and image D 57px above image C.

    Every offset is a PERCENTAGE of the column width rather than a pixel value,
    because a percentage margin resolves against the grid area's inline size —
    so the whole composition rescales without the proportions drifting. The
    bottom-row values carry a +7.2% correction measured against the rendered
    result. */}
<section class="po-exp" aria-labelledby="po-exp-title">
  <div class="u-container">
    <div class="rf">

      <div class="rf__copy">
        <p class="po-pill" data-reveal>
          <Image src={oStar} alt="" width={16} aria-hidden="true" loading="lazy" />
          <span>What actually happens</span>
        </p>
        <h2 class="rf__h" id="po-exp-title" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="70">
          Parents talk. <em>Children write.</em>
        </h2>
        <p class="rf__stand" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="140">
          The morning runs in four movements. The school photographs three of them, and publishes
          the fourth as a document.
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure class="rf__img rf__img--a" data-mask data-zoom data-zoom-to="1.07">
        <SmartImage
          file={stepPhoto[frame('a').cap ?? '']?.src}
          alt={frameAlt[frame('a').cap ?? '']}
          sizes="(max-width: 900px) 88vw, 24vw"
          fallbackWidth={1100}
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption class="rf__plate">
          {frame('a').n && (
            <span class="rf__n t-tabular">{frame('a').n}</span>
          )}
          <span class="rf__t">{frame('a').k}</span>
          <span class="rf__m">{frame('a').v}</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="rf__img rf__img--b" data-mask data-zoom data-zoom-to="1.07">
        <SmartImage
          file={stepPhoto[frame('b').cap ?? '']?.src}
          alt={frameAlt[frame('b').cap ?? '']}
          sizes="(max-width: 900px) 88vw, 24vw"
          fallbackWidth={1100}
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption class="rf__plate">
          {frame('b').n && (
            <span class="rf__n t-tabular">{frame('b').n}</span>
          )}
          <span class="rf__t">{frame('b').k}</span>
          <span class="rf__m">{frame('b').v}</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="rf__img rf__img--d" data-mask data-zoom data-zoom-to="1.07">
        <SmartImage
          file={stepPhoto[frame('d').cap ?? '']?.src}
          alt={frameAlt[frame('d').cap ?? '']}
          sizes="(max-width: 900px) 88vw, 24vw"
          fallbackWidth={1100}
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption class="rf__plate">
          {frame('d').n && (
            <span class="rf__n t-tabular">{frame('d').n}</span>
          )}
          <span class="rf__t">{frame('d').k}</span>
          <span class="rf__m">{frame('d').v}</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="rf__img rf__img--c" data-mask data-zoom data-zoom-to="1.07">
        <SmartImage
          file={stepPhoto[frame('c').cap ?? '']?.src}
          alt={frameAlt[frame('c').cap ?? '']}
          sizes="(max-width: 900px) 88vw, 24vw"
          fallbackWidth={1100}
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption class="rf__plate">
          {frame('c').n && (
            <span class="rf__n t-tabular">{frame('c').n}</span>
          )}
          <span class="rf__t">{frame('c').k}</span>
          <span class="rf__m">{frame('c').v}</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      {/* Bottom right, under columns 7–12 — the editorial close to the three
          photographic stories, where the reference put its statistics.

          ⚠ THE THREE POINTS (Understand / Connect / Participate) WERE REMOVED
          at the client's request — the panel now carries the description only.
          No verified claim is lost from the page: the paragraph keeps the staff,
          the syllabus and the curriculum-and-norms, and the 389/234 attendance
          figure is already the centrepiece of section 02.

          Previously each point traced to the official site:
            Understand   — "to get them acquainted with the curriculum and norms
                           of the school", plus the PRECEPT syllabus its own
                           photograph shows being held up in the room.
            Connect      — the one-to-one desk sessions in its photographs, and
                           parents "welcomed with smiles, guidance, and open
                           conversations".
            Participate  — 389 parents with 234 children at the first programme
                           of 2024-25, and the standing note that a family who
                           misses one is asked to join the next. */}
      <div class="tk">
        <span class="tk__glow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="tk__link" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <Image class="tk__deco" src={oStar} alt="" width={44} aria-hidden="true" loading="lazy" />

        <p class="tk__eyebrow" data-reveal>What parents take away</p>

        <h3 class="tk__h">
          <span data-clip data-clip-delay="0">A clearer</span>
          <span data-clip data-clip-delay="130"><em>beginning.</em></span>
        </h3>

        <span class="tk__rule" aria-hidden="true"><span class="tk__rule-i" data-draw></span></span>

        <p class="tk__b" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="120">
          By the time the session begins, a family has met the staff, seen the syllabus their child
          will be taught from, and had the school’s <strong>curriculum and norms</strong> set out in
          a room.
        </p>

      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{/* ══ 04 · CLOSING ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */}
<section class="po-end" aria-labelledby="po-end-title">
  <div class="po-end__media" data-zoom data-zoom-to="1.14">
    <SmartImage
      file={pDeskFamily}
      alt={ac.picAlt('pDeskFamily')}
     
      widths={[900, 1400, 1600]}
      sizes="100vw"
      loading="lazy"
      decoding="async"
    />
  </div>
  <span class="po-end__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></span>

  <div class="u-container po-end__grid">
    <div class="po-end__lead">
      <p class="po-eyebrow po-eyebrow--onink" data-reveal>The journey continues</p>
      <h2 class="po-end__h" id="po-end-title">
        <span data-drift="24">A school journey</span>
        <span data-drift="24">starts with a</span>
        <span data-drift="24"><em>conversation.</em></span>
      </h2>
    </div>

    {/* A card lifted off the photograph, carrying the school's own sentence —
        rather than a paragraph floating on the image. */}
    <div class="po-end__card" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="140">
      <blockquote class="po-end__quote">
        <p>“A warm beginning to a new academic journey. Parents were welcomed with smiles,
        guidance, and <em>open conversations</em>.”</p>
        <cite>Sunbeam School Ballia, on its first orientation of 2026-27</cite>
      </blockquote>

      <p class="po-end__b">
        The school publishes the dates, the classes, the attendance and the result of every
        programme it runs. It does not publish the agenda of the morning itself — how long it
        lasts, what the children are asked, or how a family books a place.
      </p>

      <div class="po-end__acts">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href={`tel:${school.phone.admissions}`}>
          Admissions · {school.phone.admissionsDisplay}
        </a>
        <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="/contact-us/">Contact the school</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* ⚠ ONE RHYTHM CONSTANT FOR THE WHOLE PAGE. The previous version set padding
     per section and drifted into 200px+ voids between unrelated elements. Every
     band below uses this, so vertical rhythm is one decision rather than four. */
  .po-open,
  .po-num { padding-block: clamp(52px, 6.4vw, 96px); }

  /* ⚠ TIGHTER THAN ITS SIBLINGS, ON PURPOSE. This section carries a four-frame
     composition and a panel; measured at 1127px it ran past the viewport on
     every screen under 1080 tall. Its own padding is the cheapest height to
     give back — the frames and the panel keep theirs. */
  .po-exp { padding-block: clamp(28px, 2.5vw, 42px); }

  .po-eyebrow {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 11.5px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--sb-violet);
  }

  .po-lede {
    max-width: 54ch;
    margin: clamp(16px, 2vw, 24px) 0 0;
    font-size: clamp(16px, 1.2vw, 19px);
    line-height: 1.68;
    color: var(--sb-charcoal);
  }
  .po-body {
    max-width: 54ch;
    margin: clamp(12px, 1.4vw, 18px) 0 0;
    font-size: clamp(14.5px, 1.05vw, 16px);
    line-height: 1.74;
    color: var(--sb-text-secondary);
  }
  .po-lede strong { font-weight: 700; }
  .po-lede em, .po-body em { font-style: italic; color: var(--sb-charcoal); }

  /* ═══ 01 · OPEN ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
  .po-open { background: var(--sb-ivory); }
  .po-open__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.04fr);
    gap: clamp(28px, 4.4vw, 68px);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .po-open__h {
    margin: clamp(14px, 1.8vw, 22px) 0 0;
    font-family: var(--sb-font-display);
    font-size: clamp(34px, 4.8vw, 72px);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.0;
    letter-spacing: -0.047em;
    color: var(--sb-charcoal);
  }
  .po-open__h span { display: block; }
  .po-open__h em { font-style: normal; color: var(--sb-violet); }

  /* The school's own sentence, given the weight of a pull-quote rather than
     being buried mid-paragraph. */
  .po-quote {
    position: relative;
    margin: clamp(20px, 2.6vw, 30px) 0 0;
    padding-left: clamp(16px, 2vw, 24px);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--sb-violet);
  }
  .po-quote p {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--sb-font-display);
    font-size: clamp(18px, 1.8vw, 26px);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--sb-charcoal);
  }
  .po-quote em { font-style: normal; color: var(--sb-violet); }
  .po-quote cite {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-style: normal;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: var(--sb-text-secondary);
  }

  .po-open__media { position: relative; }
  /* ⚠ A CSS MASK, NOT AN <Image>. Importing dot-bg.png through astro:assets
     handed that file to the image pipeline and made it emit as .webp — so the
     raw .png stopped being emitted and every CSS url() to it began 404-ing, on
     Academic Structure and the sports Ladder as well as here. Two other
     components already reference this artwork by URL; this one now does too, so
     the shared asset keeps exactly one owner. */
  .po-open__dots {
    position: absolute;
    top: -18px;
    right: clamp(-18px, -1.4vw, -6px);
    width: clamp(150px, 24vw, 300px);
    aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    background: var(--sb-violet);
    opacity: 0.16;
    z-index: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
    -webkit-mask-image: url('../../assets/icons/dot-bg.png');
    mask-image: url('../../assets/icons/dot-bg.png');
    -webkit-mask-size: contain;
    mask-size: contain;
    -webkit-mask-repeat: no-repeat;
    mask-repeat: no-repeat;
  }

  .po-open__frame {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    margin: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: var(--sb-r-3);
    aspect-ratio: 3 / 2;
    box-shadow: 0 40px 80px -44px rgba(27, 21, 18, 0.55);
  }
  .po-open__frame :global(picture) { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; }
  .po-open__frame :global(img) { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; }
  /* ⚠ THE CAPTION CLEARS THE INSET, AND THAT IS WHY IT IS RIGHT-ALIGNED. The
     inset frame overlaps this frame's bottom-left corner; a full-width caption
     put live text directly underneath it and the first word was unreadable.
     Only images and ornament may overlap — never an image and a text run. The
